															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cryonicautumn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4899605); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4899605&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606380109" alt="CryonicAutumn" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4899605)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cryonicautumn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4899605); return false;" >CryonicAutumn</a></span> <span class="odate time_1549314855 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">04 Feb 2019 21:14</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4141780">
									

<p>This ended up being pretty long for a discussion post, so the history is in the collapsible for those who are curious.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Open&nbsp;textdump</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close&nbsp;textdump</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Before the final draft, before the crappy first draft, before I even had an account on this site I had a thought: what would happen to somebody stuck forever in a single room? This concept developed to the idea of an empty pocket dimension where immortality is guaranteed and escape is impossible, along with the temporal distortions to have the subject both experience a near eternity and be able to communicate with the outside world.</p>
<p>The main differences (besides basic quality increases) between the current version and the original version were that SCP-4903 was originally a painting and the temporal distortions were under the control of SCP-4903-2. I changed it from a painting because weird paintings are boring and done to death, and I changed the distortions to something chaotic and uncontrollable to fit with the feel of the article.</p>
<p>Researcher Elmsway was a result of my desire to hold a more concrete foil to the Foundation. I had the idea in mind that the effect of SCP-4903 would create a living testament to the failings of the Foundation method of sending D-Class on early exploratory missions into anomalies, and initially Elmsway was just the name of the device that was used in the incident log. I ended up liking the name and kept him as the Foundation side of the story, a scientist who can see the failings of his work but also who knows that there was no other feasible way to test the danger of new anomalies to humans. I surmised that SCP-4903-2 would be able to come to the same conclusion. I also thought that SCP-4903-2 being friendly and joking while holding a mostly nihilistic outlook would be the most effective for the story. Remember, this is someone who gets around a week of human interaction per every couple thousand years.</p>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close&nbsp;textdump</a></div>
</div>
</div>
<p>I also added a hint of another concept, but I made sure the article worked without it. I would recommend opening the spoiler only after reading the article completely.</p>
<p>There's another effect at play here, but on the advice of Weryllium I'm removing the spoiler for it so you'll have to figure it out yourself ;)</p>

