			<div class="content" id="post-content-4143103">
									

<p>This is nice.</p>
<p>The D-class is good, and a dark parallel to characters such as 11424, where in this case the rapport is still there but the exploration isn't a happy ending. I also like that you avoided making him a one-dimensional &quot;arrrghhh i'm angry at the Foundation&quot; cliche.</p>
<p>Project Timaeus is <em>insanely</em> creative in concept, kudos for that.</p>
<p>Personally, I prefer the article without the spoiler, guess that's Death of the Author. My impression when reading was that the effect would happen through purely nonanomalous means; Elmsway isn't going to be there forever, whether via transfer, amnesticization, or even plain old death. One day there'll be a containment breach, or an attack on the Site, or a K-class scenario, or just the simple ravages of bureaucracy, and 4903-2 will eventually be forgotten and alone. Forever.</p>
<p>Excellent work.</p>

							</div>

								
					
